-- title:
--   Rank of a truncated polynomial algebra over a finite index set
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a nontrivial commutative ring, $\iota$ a finite type, and $N \colon \iota \to \mathbb{N}$ a family of exponents. Consider the polynomial ring $k[X_i : i \in \iota]$ in the variables indexed by $\iota$ and the ideal generated by the set of powers $X_i^{N_i}$ for $i \in \iota$ (the range of the map $i \mapsto X_i^{N_i}$). The assertion is that the $k$-module rank, in the sense of `Module.finrank`, of the quotient $k[X_i : i \in \iota] / (X_i^{N_i} : i \in \iota)$ equals $\prod_{i \in \iota} N_i$, the product being taken over all of $\iota$. Note that only the numerical rank is asserted, not the freeness of the quotient nor the explicit monomial basis; and when some $N_i = 0$ the ideal is the unit ideal, the quotient vanishes and both sides are $0$, consistently with the convention that `finrank` is $0$ for modules with no finite basis.
--
--   This is the standard computation of the $k$-rank of a truncated polynomial algebra $k[X_i]/(X_i^{N_i})$, the monomials in the box $\{m : m_i < N_i\}$ accounting for the product $\prod_i N_i$. It is used to read off the order of a finite flat group scheme whose coordinate ring is presented in this shape, namely in [`HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_mvPolynomial_quotient_X_pow_of_isNilpotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_mvPolynomial_quotient_X_pow_of_isNilpotent).
